    {
      "question": "The nursing home (Park View) appears only in the all-fund budget-and-actual schedule (Nursing Home revenues 3,761,937; Public buildings - nursing home 3,760,166), not in the audited governmental or proprietary fund statements. Should it be counted as a business-type fund of the village or left out as a separate entity?",
      "amount": 3761937,
      "recorded_as": "detail only, fund Nursing Home, business-type, patient service revenue / hospital/health care (not in receipts, disbursements or business_type)",
      "source_page": 9
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Modified cash basis. Governmental receipts/disbursements from the Totals column of the governmental funds statement (p5); the roll-forward uses fund balance (544,662 to 402,864, p6) as cash. Net transfers (118) in the Totals column recorded as transfers_out 118; Loan to Nursing Home (46,000) recorded as other_financing. Taxes and Intergovernmental split using the General Fund combining schedule (p10) and statement of activities (p3); Street fund taxes 24,698 are franchise fees (Statement of Activities franchise fees 77,086 less General Fund 52,388; inferred, marked review); Street/Debt Service intergovernmental have no printed breakdown. Business-type: operating revenues 357,206 plus no nonoperating revenues; Charges for services 357,156 split by fund column (p8) into Utility Charges 301,252 (Sewer, Water, Sanitation) and Ambulance Fees 55,904; nonoperating (expenses) capital 47,387, principal 30,631, interest 13,582 treated as disbursements; total disbursements 350,797 printed on p2 (259,197 + 91,600). Business-type roll-forward 238,279 + 357,206 - 350,797 + 118 = 244,806. Business-type operating expense lines split by fund column so the Ambulance fund (37,806) is public safety and Sewer/Water/Sanitation are utilities. Balance sheet from government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1), total column; no liabilities printed. Detail: General Fund combining schedule (p10) used instead of the p9 combined budget schedule (all-fund types, includes nursing home) to avoid double counting, except the Nursing Home revenues 3,761,937 and Public buildings - nursing home 3,760,166 lines, which appear on no other schedule and are recorded from p9 as a business-type Nursing Home fund (no separate printed total); business-type detail covers operating lines only (nonoperating lines are in main disbursements); the proprietary statement lines already in detail are kept (existing lines kept per user rule). Governmental net position per p1 totals 402,864 matches fund balance. Community Building department spending is general government (p5 General government 110,684 = General 86,988 + Community Building 23,696). Attempt 2 (2026-10-28 verifier fixes): notes order fixed, business-type charges for services split into Utility Charges / Ambulance Fees, Ambulance detail revenue category Ambulance Fees, intergovernmental 'Other' labels as printed (heading in department). Attempt 3 (2026-10-29 audit fix): the nursing home (Park View) is not a fund in the basic statements (it only receives a 46,000 loan); the p9 budget schedule's cash balances exceed the statements' by exactly the nursing home's net (1,771 change), so its two p9 detail lines are marked outside_statement: true and excluded from receipts/disbursements/business_type (no double counting). Read pages 1-10 of 10"
}
